int bc_observe_unsubscribe(bc_client_t *c);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unsubscribes the client from command observation events on
\f[CR]CHAN_OBSERVE\f[R] (channel 3).
This is equivalent to calling
\f[CR]bc_observe_subscribe(c, BC_OBSERVE_LEVEL_OFF)\f[R].
.PP
After unsubscribing, the server stops generating \f[CR]pre_command\f[R]
and \f[CR]post_command\f[R] events for this session.
Any events already in the client\(cqs receive buffer are discarded on
the next \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] call.
.PP
Registered callbacks are \f[B]not\f[R] removed by this function.
They remain in place so that re\-subscribing later will resume delivery
without needing to re\-register callbacks.
To explicitly remove callbacks, pass NULL to
\f[CR]bc_observe_on_pre_command()\f[R] or
\f[CR]bc_observe_on_post_command()\f[R].
.PP
Calling \f[CR]bc_observe_unsubscribe()\f[R] when not currently
subscribed is a no\-op and returns \f[CR]BC_OK\f[R].
